hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"287","A chapter on horses and riding animals: Hannad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Rashid, he said: It was said to Makhul: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim did not allot shares to horses from the fortress of Tustar - a fortress he had conquered. So Makhul said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted shares to horses on the day of Khaybar, though it was only a fortress."
"288","Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, al-Nu'man informed me, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted on the day of Khaybar two shares to the horses, one share to the footman, one share to the children, and one share to the women."
"289","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from a man of the people of Makkah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided an expedition and they gained booty, so he allotted to the horseman three shares, to the footman one share, and to the mailed (armored) fighter two shares."
"290","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from al-Zubayr, meaning Ibn al-Khirrit, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a horse, so he went to it and wiped its face, its eyes and its nostrils with the sleeve of his shirt. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, do you wipe with the sleeve of your shirt? He said: Gabriel has reproached me concerning horses."
"291","Al-Walid ibn Utbah narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Ali ibn Hawshab narrated to us; he heard Makhul saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wipe (and rub) the horses and cover them with cloths."
"292","Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah and Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us, from Masarrah ibn Ma'bad, from al-Wadin - Muhammad ibn Sulayman said: al-Wadin ibn Ata' - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not lead horses by their forelocks so as to humiliate them."
"293","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Wa'il - or Bakr ibn Wa'il - from al-Zuhri, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Delay the loads, for hands are suspended and feet are shackled."
